WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.380
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.150
TULSEE DOSHI: So my top
career tip for women in tech

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:13.240
is to surround yourself
with incredible role models.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:14.920
I think one of the
best things that I've

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.370
found for myself in my career at
Google and my career at Broadly

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.590
has been learning from
and surrounding myself

00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:23.770
with incredibly smart,
talented, motivated people.

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:27.940
And these are people who
lift me up, who champion me,

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:31.150
and who give me the opportunity
to champion and lift up others.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.520
STEPHANIE WONG: Know how to
overcome imposter syndrome.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:37.900
I face it every day, but I
have learned to really focus

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:39.262
on the value that I bring.

00:00:39.262 --> 00:00:41.470
Maybe you're scared that
you're not technical enough,

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:45.160
or you don't fit this idea of
what someone in tech should be.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:47.120
But that changes
every single day,

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:48.562
and we're redefining
it as women.

00:00:48.562 --> 00:00:50.020
RACHEL BEEN: Bring
your whole self.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:53.440
Don't worry about what "in
tech" is supposed to mean.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.180
I used to be a
photographer, used

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:59.380
to shoot a lot of concerts
in a pit with a lot of men.

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:02.350
And what I learned by
navigating that scenario

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:06.120
I feel like it's very applicable
to my day to day life now.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:10.030
RACHEL INMAN: A career tip that
I feel like has been told to me

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:12.100
and that I've tried to
pass along to others

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:15.460
is this idea of
following your curiosity.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:20.560
So rather than mapping out
a perfect five year plan

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:24.310
or pursuing a particular
title, more so

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:27.850
kind of paying attention to that
little voice inside your head

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:30.820
that says something
is really interesting.

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:34.127
And kind of pursuing projects
that feed that curiosity.

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:35.710
DALE MARKOWITZ: When
you work in tech,

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:38.180
you are so lucky
for many reasons.

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:41.140
But one is that so many
fields and articles

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:42.320
can benefit from tech.

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:44.050
So advantage number
one is that you

00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:45.580
can work in so many
different fields

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:47.440
and on so many
different problems.

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:48.940
And of course,
advantage number two

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:50.565
is that if you work
in tech because you

00:01:50.565 --> 00:01:53.740
have this unique perspective
that's so valuable,

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:54.970
you're very hirable.

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:56.720
You can work in a lot
of different places.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.095
ALEXANDRINA
GARCIA-VERDIN: I have

00:01:58.095 --> 00:02:00.910
a tip on how to overcome
the "I'm not enough"

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:03.970
fear when applying
to your dream job.

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:07.850
The solution is building a
skills-based resume rather than

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:09.470
a timeline.

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:11.662
Empathy has taught me
that people need to really

00:02:11.662 --> 00:02:13.870
quickly understand if they
should call a candidate up

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:17.560
or not within the first 30
seconds of reviewing a resume.

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:21.100
So really save your detailed
experiences for interviews

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:23.650
and only share a
few relevant items

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:26.768
that make employers curious
to learn more about you.

00:02:26.768 --> 00:02:28.810
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: My one
tip for women in tech--

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:31.180
just don't be afraid of
trying different technologies

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:31.960
and roles.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.060
You might surprise
yourself with what you find

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:35.080
and what you like.

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:37.810
SHILPA VIR: Get comfortable
talking about your work.

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:42.760
So many of us have this mental
hurdle of, am I bragging?

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:44.000
Is it too much?

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.550
Should I be talking
about myself?

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:47.800
Shouldn't my work be
talking about myself?

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:51.220
But the reality is we are
great cheerleaders of others.

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:53.770
We talk at length about
their accomplishments.

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:57.193
And we need to be equally good
at talking about our own work.

00:02:57.193 --> 00:02:59.110
ALICIA WILLIAMS: To value
your own perspective

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.240
and remind yourself often.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:03.930
It's super easy to get
into that comparison trap,

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:06.460
but a difference
is not a weakness.

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:09.120
SIFO LUO: If you're not happy
with the current way of working

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.520
or with the culture
of our society,

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:14.740
and you want to be the one
to initiate the change,

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:17.020
my strategy is to
set your mindset

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:21.940
to be curious and optimistic
and stay persistent with what

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:22.673
you believe.

00:03:22.673 --> 00:03:24.090
SWETHA SRINIVASAN:
Embrace changes

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:27.310
as they come, and be prepared
for any opportunities that

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:28.270
may come by.

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:31.570
So that you're always ready
to take on new opportunities.

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:32.770
ESRA KUCUKOGUZ: Do not fear.

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:33.970
Be brave.

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:36.070
Women belong in tech.

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:38.170
Do not let anyone make
you think otherwise.

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:40.320
